\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Method pipeline. The net-load fit, which needs only data the DSO holds, supplies the sensitivities $s_h$, $s_c$ and the thresholds $T_h$, $T_c$; the SF fit of a submetered pilot supplies only the SF sensitivities $m_h$, $m_c$. Their ratio gives the installed capacity per regime. The net-load fit alone gives the temperature-driven energy, and the capacity with the transferred sensitivity gives the flexibility.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pipeline}{{1}{3}{Method pipeline. The net-load fit, which needs only data the DSO holds, supplies the sensitivities $s_h$, $s_c$ and the thresholds $T_h$, $T_c$; the SF fit of a submetered pilot supplies only the SF sensitivities $m_h$, $m_c$. Their ratio gives the installed capacity per regime. The net-load fit alone gives the temperature-driven energy, and the capacity with the transferred sensitivity gives the flexibility}{figure.1}{}}
